Z||000000||85ZainoGT||11-11-2001||10:08 PM||||well... I just need to know how to do a few things and I need to know a few things..<BR>  1. My brakes are squeaking, how do I fix/check that deal?<BR>  2. the 2 vents in the corners of the trunk lid.. one side doesnt have any screws holding it down.. can I just go buy screws anywhere? what size?<BR>  3. my car as rear defrost, I should be able to tint my back window still right? someone told me its not good too...<BR>  4. when I turn the wheel almost all the way either way, I hear a sound, maybe rubbing? is this possible? common?<BR>  5. could I just take my 2.8 out and slap a 3.4 in there for less than 1000 dollar bills? because the 2.8 has 136k on it.. <P>I think that is it for now... thanks <BR><P>------------------<BR>Paul Ventimiglia<BR>1987 Gold GT 2.8L<BR>All the options :)<BR>  pics are coming :)||||reg||1
Z||000001||Pheagey||11-11-2001||10:16 PM||||Brakes: Squeaking hua. Weel make sure u have a good amount of gbrake pad left. Outside of theat get diffrant pads.\<BR>Vent screws: check the local pick-n-pull (salavge yard). should be able to get a four real cheap ( paint them yup w/ some spray paint and ur all set.<BR>tint: Dunno 'bout that one.<BR>Rubbing noise:Get it greased up and check the bushings. Also check under the car for anything 'unusual'.<BR>3.4 Engine: If you do most of the work urself and have the place/tools, probly. Other wise not a chance.<P>Welcome ot the forum...<BR><P>------------------<BR>'88 coupe, 5 speed.<BR>"The car formerly know as Dj's Fiero."||||reg||2
Z||000002||avengador1||11-11-2001||10:31 PM||||If you tint the rear window put in a light tint. I bought my car with dark tint and it's a real b**ch to see out the back at night. Make sure your rear brake cable is not too tight. This will make the rear pads rub and squeak. hope this helps.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||11-12-2001||09:17 AM||||I wouldn't worry too much about the screws for the vents.  One of the previous owners put the wrong screw in the passenger side vent on my '86 GT.  I took it out a few months ago and haven't had any trouble yet.||||reg||1
